    "X3 V2 uses the KC2-owned Choc V2/PG1353 bottom-side hot-swap socket plus Cherry MX 5-pin direct-solder geometry.",
    "Choc V1 switch geometry, Choc V2 direct-solder pads, and MX hot-swap socket pads are intentionally excluded.",
    "The Choc socket and MX switch are mutually exclusive assembly options at every key position.",
    "X3 V2 uses the fixed 70-key v5 no-stabilizer layout: 31 left keys and 39 right keys, with no key wider than 1.75U.",
    "X3 V2 insets every non-controller key-field edge 1.5 mm from the nominal switch-cell perimeter. Rows 0-3 use 8.025 mm center-to-edge offsets on both sides; bottom Space-B uses 15.16875 mm left / 8.02500 mm right.",
    "X3 V2 contains no legacy H1-H9 or REG1-REG9 key-field through-holes.",
    "The netless battery-lead slot is at the nice!nano USB/B+ end; insulated B+ and GND/B- leads must use strain relief and remain outside the antenna keepout.",
    "X3 V2 uses the exact Jingdao ES1B / LCSC C437840 / Eleparts 9475342 manufacturer-recommended SMA land on B.Cu: 1.8 x 1.8 mm pads, 2.4 mm inner gap, pin 1 cathode to row and pin 2 anode to the per-key switch net.",
    "The ES1B placements and rotations preserve at least 1.30 mm to Edge.Cuts, 1.00 mm to switch copper/unused NPTH/unrelated exposed copper, and one unobstructed 1.50 mm cardinal hand-solder approach per pad.",
    "X3 V2 uses the selected 8-left / 10-right M1.4 retention prototype: 1.60 mm copper-free NPTHs, keycaps removed and switches installed for PH0 service. Physical pilot, torque, full-pattern fit, and deflection evidence remain pending; the board is not order-ready."
